From: RDK Build Compatibility
Subject: [PATCH] bash: return correctly from POSIX signal handlers

POSIX signal handlers return void. Use a bare return when POSIX signals are
enabled, even when VOID_SIGHANDLER was not separately detected.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/sig.h
+++ b/sig.h
@@ -35 +35 @@
-#if defined (VOID_SIGHANDLER)
+#if defined (VOID_SIGHANDLER) || defined (HAVE_POSIX_SIGNALS)
